%I A399265 #22 Sep 23 2026 18:40:57
%S A399265 24,72,120,144,240,336,360,504,672,720,840,864,1008,1080,1200,1320,
%T A399265 1440,1584,1800,1872,2016,2160,2184,2400,2520,2880,3264,3360,3600,
%U A399265 3672,3696,3960,4104,4320,4560,4896,5040,5280,5400,5544,6048,6072,6240,6552,6600,6624
%N A399265 Numbers having two factor pairs whose absolute pairwise differences form the legs of a primitive Pythagorean triple.
%C A399265 Every term of the sequence is divisible by 24.
%C A399265 Terms are of the form A094807(m)*A002378(k), for m>=1 and k>=1.
%C A399265 All terms are k*(k+1)*l1*l2 for any k > 1, where l1 and l2 are the legs of the triple. Every primitive Pythagorean triple contains one leg which is divisible by 3 and one leg which is divisible by 4 and k*(k+1) must be even. Therefore, every term of the sequence is divisible by 24.
%H A399265 Russ Curry, <a href="/A399265/b399265.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A399265 The number 24 has two factor pairs, (3, 8) and (6, 4), with absolute pairwise differences |3-6| and |8-4|, forming the legs of the (3, 4, 5) triple.
%e A399265 The number 120 has two factor pairs, (5, 24) and (10, 12), with absolute pairwise differences |5-10| and |24-12|, forming the legs of the (5, 12, 13) triple.
%o A399265 (Python)
%o A399265 from math import isqrt, gcd
%o A399265 from sympy import divisors
%o A399265 terms = 100
%o A399265 results = []
%o A399265 n = 1
%o A399265 while len(results) < terms:
%o A399265     f = divisors(n)
%o A399265     for index, i in enumerate(f):
%o A399265         for j in f[:index]:
%o A399265             x, y = j - i, n // j - n // i
%o A399265             z = x*x + y*y
%o A399265             if isqrt(z)**2 == z and gcd(x, y) == 1:
%o A399265                 results.append(n)
%o A399265                 break
%o A399265         else:
%o A399265             continue
%o A399265         break
%o A399265     n += 1
%o A399265 print("\n".join(str(v) for v in results))
%Y A399265 Subsequence of A008606.
%Y A399265 Cf. A020882, A020883, A020884.
%Y A399265 Cf. A094807, A002378.
%K A399265 nonn,new
%O A399265 1,1
%A A399265 _Russ Curry_, Aug 25 2026
